{
    "background_story": "Alicia was a renowned paleontologist with a passion for the ancient world of saurischian dinosaurs. Growing up, she spent hours poring over dusty tomes and exploring fossil beds, fascinated by the long-necked, herbivorous sauropods and the fierce, carnivorous theropods. Her groundbreaking research on the evolution of saurischian hips led to a major breakthrough in the field, earning her the coveted Golden Fossil Award. Alicia's expertise took her to the badlands of Argentina, where she led an expedition to uncover the remains of a previously unknown sauropod species. Her team's discoveries shed new light on the diversity of saurischian dinosaurs during the Mesozoic era. Alicia's work continues to inspire a new generation of paleontologists, fueling their own quests to uncover the secrets of the ancient world.",
